.TH "waybar\-mango\-language" "5" "2026\-08\-07"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- mango language module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBlanguage\fR module displays the currently active keyboard layout in the Mango compositor.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBmango/language\fR
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: {} 
.br
The format, how the layout should be displayed.\& See \fBFORMAT REPLACEMENTS\fR.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-<lang>\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Provide an alternative format string for a given language.\&
.RS 4
<lang> is the short description of the layout (e.\&g.\& "us", "de").\&
The value is used as the replacement for \fB{}\fR in the main \fBformat\fR.\&
This option can be repeated for multiple languages.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBformat\-<lang>\-<variant>\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Like \fBformat\-<lang>\fR but also matches the layout variant, taking precedence over \fBformat\-<lang>\fR when both the language and variant match.\&
.PP
\fBmenu\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Action that pops up a menu.\&
.PP
\fBmenu\-file\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Location of the menu descriptor file.\& It must contain an element of type GtkMenu with id \fBmenu\fR.\&
.PP
\fBmenu\-actions\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
Actions corresponding to the buttons of the menu.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables this module to consume all leftover space dynamically.\&
.PP
.SH FORMAT REPLACEMENTS
.PP
\fB{short}\fR: Short name of the layout (e.\&g.\& "us").\&
.PP
\fB{shortDescription}\fR: Short description of the layout (same as \fB{short}\fR in most cases).\&
.PP
\fB{long}\fR: Full name of the layout as reported by Mango (e.\&g.\& "English (US)").\& The empty positional \fB{}\fR in the default format resolves to this value, so the long name is shown when no \fBformat\fR is specified.\&
.PP
\fB{variant}\fR: Variant of the layout, if any.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"mango/language": {
	"format": " {long} ",
	"format\-us": "US",
	"format\-de": "DE"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH STYLE
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#language\fR
.PD
.PP
A CSS class matching the current layout'\&s short name is added to the widget.\&
This allows per‑layout styling:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
#language\&.us { color: #00ff00; }
#language\&.de { color: #ff0000; }
.fi
.RE
